[0;34m==>[0m Part 3: Deduplication (Store Once, Reference Many)
[0;35m🎯[0m Testing deduplication with duplicate data
[0;36m→[0m Storing duplicate files...
[0;32m✓[0m 5 files stored (identical content)

[0;36m→[0m Without deduplication:
  • 5 files × 60 bytes = 300 bytes stored
[0;36m→[0m With deduplication:
  • Physical storage: 60 bytes (1 copy)
  • Logical storage: 300 bytes (5 references)
  • Dedup ratio: 5.0x
  • Space saved: 240 bytes (80%)

[0;35m🎯[0m Deduplication Best For:
  ✓ VM images (90% identical)
  ✓ Backup storage
  ✓ User documents (many duplicates)
  ✗ Unique data (no benefit)
  ✗ High write workloads (overhead)

[0;34m==>[0m Part 4: Copy-on-Write (Data Safety)
[0;35m🎯[0m Understanding Copy-on-Write (COW)

Traditional Filesystem:
  1. Read old data
  2. Overwrite with new data ← DANGER!
  3. If crash here → corruption

ZFS Copy-on-Write:
  1. Write new data to new location
  2. Update pointer ← Atomic!
  3. Free old data
  → Never corrupts, always consistent

[0;36m→[0m COW Benefits:
  ✓ Atomic operations (all or nothing)
  ✓ No fsck needed (ever!)
  ✓ Snapshots are nearly free
  ✓ Data integrity guaranteed

[0;32m✓[0m NestGate leverages COW for safe operations

[0;34m==>[0m Part 5: Real-World Usage Examples
[0;35m🎯[0m Example 1: Safe Software Updates
    # Before update
    curl -X POST ${NESTGATE_URL}/api/v1/datasets/app/snapshots \
      -d '{"name": "before-update"}'
    
    # Do update
    ./update.sh
    
    # If problems:
    curl -X POST ${NESTGATE_URL}/api/v1/datasets/app/rollback \
      -d '{"snapshot": "before-update"}'

[0;35m🎯[0m Example 2: Efficient Backups
    # Daily snapshots (instant, free!)
    0 0 * * * curl -X POST ${NESTGATE_URL}/api/v1/datasets/data/snapshots \
      -d '{"name": "daily-'$(date +%Y%m%d)'"}'
    
    # Keep 30 days, delete old
    # Only changed blocks use space!

[0;35m🎯[0m Example 3: Testing Environments
    # Production data
    curl -X POST ${NESTGATE_URL}/api/v1/datasets/production/snapshots \
      -d '{"name": "latest"}'
    
    # Clone for testing (instant, cheap!)
    curl -X POST ${NESTGATE_URL}/api/v1/datasets/production/clone \
      -d '{"snapshot": "latest", "target": "test"}'
    
    # Test destructively, no risk to production!

